  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> represents the total fence area, in square feet. Since the fence will be stained twice, the amount of stain, in gallons, will need to cover <math alttext=\"2 w\"><mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> square feet. It&rsquo;s also given that one gallon of stain will cover <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> square feet. Dividing the total area, in square feet, of the surface to be stained by the number of square feet covered by one gallon of stain gives the number of gallons of stain that will be needed. Dividing <math alttext=\"2 w\"><mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> yields &nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 2 w Over 170 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow><mn>170</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"StartFraction w Over 85 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>w</mi><mn>85</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the equation that represents the total amount of stain <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math>, in gallons, needed to stain the fence of the yard twice is <math alttext=\"upper S equals StartFraction w Over 85 EndFraction\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>w</mi><mn>85</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>",
